s yield sets f.Suspended first)."] [219 1 "// opImpls are the operations registered by the files that own them (§9), each by its file's init:"] [220 1 "// RegisterOp(OpLoadAttr, ...). An operation of step's switch is never looked up here."] [223 1 "// RegisterOp sets op's implementation; a second one is a programming error (one owner per operation)."] [231 1 "// pushFrame is step's signal that the instruction called a Python function: not an exception."] [234 1 "// callStack is call [N KWNAMES]: the callable under its N arguments on f's stack (the last len(kwnames) of them"] [235 1 "// keywords), all popped; a Python function's frame (a bound method's, its self first) made from the arguments"] [236 1 "// where they are on the stack and returned as the thread's *pushFrame, a generator made, or any other callable"] [237 1 "// called and its value pushed (202b: the arguments were copied off the stack, then again with self in front)."] [241 22 "// sys.monitoring's CALL, C_RETURN, C_RAISE (queue 220)"] [253 24 "// the callable's slot holds self: the arguments are self's and the stack's"] [266 4 "// a built-in method bound to its object (BuiltinType's call slot): its arguments made at once with self"] [267 4 "// first (queue 210: they were copied off the stack, then again behind self)"] [283 51 "// next(gen()): the generator dies at the return (queue 297)"] [306 3 "// CPython's RETURN_GENERATOR: the frame kept in its generator, coroutine or async generator"] [315 1 "// directMax bounds the direct calls (callDirect) nested on the thread's Go stack at once: each holds its caller's Go"] [316 1 "// frames while its callee runs, so a deeper chain (a recursion past it, up to any recursion limit) goes on as pushed"] [317 1 "// frames, in the innermost loop, with no Go frames per Python call (queue 216d)."] [320 1 "// enter is a call's callee frame (made, its arguments bound) run from f: when f and the callee are both compiled,"] [321 1 "// directly by f's own Go code (callDirect